==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|acceptible||dated}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*keh₂p-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|acceptable}}, from {{der|en|fro|acceptable}}, from {{der|en|LL.|acceptābilis|t=worthy of acceptance}}.

Morphologically {{af|en|accept|-able}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əkˈsɛp.tə.bəl/|/ækˈsɛp.tə.bəl/|/ɪkˈsɛp.tə.bəl/}}
* {{i|obsolete}} {{IPA|en|/ˈæksɛp.tə.bəl/}}<ref>{{R:Jespersen MEGoHP|I|5.66|170}}</ref>
* {{audio|en|en-us-acceptable.ogg|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{1|worthy}}, [[decent]], sure of being [[accept]]ed or received with at least moderate [[pleasure]].
#: {{ux|en|We need to find an '''acceptable''' present for Jeff.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1883|author=United States. War Department|title=Annual Reports of the War Department|volume=1|page=128
|passage=I think if post commanders of the unchaplained posts could employ '''acceptable''' clergymen {{...}} then the needs might be met.}}
# Barely worthy, less than excellent; [[passable]].
#: {{ux|en|The designs were '''acceptable''', but they were nothing special either.}}

