===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Someone or something that is [[#Adjective|acceptable]].
#: {{ant|en|rejectable#Noun}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Madhusūdan Kaul|chapter=Introduction|title=Sri Mālinīvijayottara Tantram|series=Kashmir Series of Texts and Studies|seriesvolume=XXXVII|location=Bombay|publisher={{...|Printed at the}} “Tatva-vivechaka” Press|year=1922|page=xvii|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.228520/page/n21/mode/1up|passage=The whole range of the knowable is divided into two classes, the acceptable and the avoidable. The '''acceptables''' are: Śiva, Śakti, Vidyesa, Mantra, Mantreśvara and the Jivas.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Harry Alan Potamkin|chapter=A Diet of Stars|editor=w:Lewis Jacobs|title=The Compound Cinema: The Film Writings of Harry Alan Potamkin|series=Studies in Culture & Communication|location=New York, N.Y.&#59; London|publisher=w:Teachers College Press|start_year=c. 1929|year=1930|year_published=1977|section=part 3 (Miscellany), section 9 (Other Writings)|page=565|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/compoundcinemafi0000pota/page/565/mode/1up|isbn=0-8077-1559-X|passage=The good old '''acceptables''' are called “character” actors. An actor of the versatile order is called, casually, even contemptuously, a “character” actor.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Henry Klein|title=The Dental Status and Dental Needs of Young Adult Males, Rejectable or Acceptable for Military Service, According to Selective Service Dental Requirements|journal=w:Public Health Reports|volume=56|issue=27|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=w:United States Public Health Service|date=4 July 1941|pages=1373–1374|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sim_public-health-reports_1941-07-04_56_27/page/1374/mode/1up|passage=Close to 3 percent of the '''acceptables''' are free of DMF teeth while none of the rejectables have fewer than 7 DMF teeth.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Ray Wells|title=The Church and the Aging|journal=The Free Will Baptist|location=Ayden, N.C.|date=19 June 1974|page=5|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/freewillbaptists89free/page/n394/mode/1up|column=3|passage=The church will not be content to see that older persons are housed and entertained, or even that '''acceptables''' are worked out to provide them with therapy and income from jobs.}}

